data: {"event": "reasoning.available", "run_id": "run_26b4c235bb9d4966b4b128ddcaf2d123", "timestamp": 1789921350.5785222, "text": "The first command to diagnose connection refused from a local HTTP server is:\n\n```bash\nnc -vz <host> <port>\n```\n\nThat runs against the real network path and reports the specific reason if the socket cannot be established.\n\nA second, more useful diagnostic is:\n\n```bash\nss -tlnp | grep <host>:<port>\n```\n\nThat confirms whether the process is bound to the interface, listening on TCP, and which PID owns it \u2014 a prerequisite before a connection can be refused."}

data: {"event": "run.completed", "run_id": "run_26b4c235bb9d4966b4b128ddcaf2d123", "timestamp": 1789921350.593076, "output": "The first command to diagnose connection refused from a local HTTP server is:\n\n```bash\nnc -vz <host> <port>\n```\n\nThat runs against the real network path and reports the specific reason if the socket cannot be established.\n\nA second, more useful diagnostic is:\n\n```bash\nss -tlnp | grep <host>:<port>\n```\n\nThat confirms whether the process is bound to the interface, listening on TCP, and which PID owns it \u2014 a prerequisite before a connection can be refused.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 14407, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 14514}}

